</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Model Identifiers</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For reproducibility, we provide the exact model identifiers used in our experiments. The models are: DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B (<span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B</span>), Qwen3-8B (<span id="A2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Qwen/Qwen3-8B</span>), Claude 3.7 (<span id="A2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">claude-3-7-sonnet-20250219</span>, accessed via the Claude API), GPT-OSS-20B (<span id="A2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">openai/gpt-oss-20b</span>), and Magistral-Small (<span id="A2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">mistralai/Magistral-Small-2509</span>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Additional Similarity Analyses</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We report the cosine similarity between the embedding of the <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th reasoning step <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and the final conclusion <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, interpolated using the maximum number of reasoning steps (Figure <a href="#A3.F1" title="Figure C.1 ‣ Appendix C Additional Similarity Analyses ‣ Lost at the Beginning of Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F1" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A3.F1.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2506.22058v3/semantic_similarity_GPT5_longest.svg" id="A3.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/380;" width="548" height="380"></object>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A3.F1.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2506.22058v3/semantic_similarity_Heuristic_longest.svg" id="A3.F1.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/380;" width="548" height="380"></object>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure C.1: </span>Cosine similarity between the embeddings of the i-th reasoning step <math id="A3.F1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and the final conclusion <math id="A3.F1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, using the maximum number of reasoning steps for interpolation. The reasoning steps are segmented either by GPT-5 (left) or by heuristic rules (right).</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In addition, we report SPLADE similarity <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Formal et al., 2021</a>)</cite>, which provides a sparse lexical–semantic relevance signal by expanding tokens into weighted lexical features. We compute SPLADE similarity using the <span id="A3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">naver/splade-cocondenser-ensembledistil</span> model <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Formal et al., 2022</a>)</cite>, following standard practice. As shown in Figure <a href="#A3.F2" title="Figure C.2 ‣ Appendix C Additional Similarity Analyses ‣ Lost at the Beginning of Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>, the trends closely mirror those observed under cosine similarity. These results serve as complementary checks, confirming that our findings are not tied to dense embedding models and hold across both dense and sparse similarity measures.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F2" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A3.F2.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2506.22058v3/splade_similarity_GPT5_mean.svg" id="A3.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/380;" width="548" height="380"></object>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A3.F2.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2506.22058v3/splade_similarity_Heuristic_mean.svg" id="A3.F2.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/380;" width="548" height="380"></object>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure C.2: </span>SPLADE similarity between the representations of the i-th reasoning step <math id="A3.F2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and the final conclusion <math id="A3.F2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, using the maximum number of reasoning steps for interpolation. The reasoning steps are segmented either by GPT-5 (left) or by heuristic rules (right).</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Correlation between first reasoning step and final prediction</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the main text, we reported results on DS-R1-Qwen-7B. Here we extend the analysis to Qwen3-8B (Figure <a href="#A4.F1" title="Figure D.1 ‣ Appendix D Correlation between first reasoning step and final prediction ‣ Lost at the Beginning of Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>) and further include DeepSeek and Qwen3 models of different sizes (Figure <a href="#A4.F2" title="Figure D.2 ‣ Appendix D Correlation between first reasoning step and final prediction ‣ Lost at the Beginning of Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>). These additional results verify that the correlation between the first reasoning step and the final prediction persists as model size scales.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F1" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F1.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2506.22058v3/first_reason_accuracy_qwen3-8b.svg" id="A4.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/343;" width="548" height="343"></object>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F1.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2506.22058v3/first_reason_number_of_tokens_qwen3_8b.svg" id="A4.F1.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/343;" width="548" height="343"></object>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure D.1: </span>Accuracy and number of tokens on Qwen3-8B. <span id="A4.F1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Left:</span> The relationship between the accuracy of the final prediction (<math id="A4.F1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>) and the correctness of the prediction solely based on the first reasoning step (<math id="A4.F1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>) across different difficulty levels. If <math id="A4.F1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is incorrect, <math id="A4.F1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is more likely incorrect. <span id="A4.F1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Right:</span> The number of tokens used for the final prediction after the first reasoning step <math id="A4.F1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., the number of tokens used for <math id="A4.F1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[t_{2},t_{3},...,t_{T}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[t_{2},t_{3},...,t_{T}]</annotation></semantics></math>. Although <math id="A4.F1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is correct, the model still consumes a large amount of tokens for the following reasoning steps–overthinking.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.F2" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2506.22058v3/first_step_accuracy_more_models.svg" id="A4.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:411/241;" width="411" height="241"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure D.2: </span>More results from Qwen and DeepSeek models of different sizes. We report the relationship between the accuracy of the final prediction (<math id="A4.F2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>) and the correctness of the first reasoning step (<math id="A4.F2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>). If <math id="A4.F2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is incorrect, <math id="A4.F2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is more likely to be incorrect.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Prompt Examples</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The template for using the DeepSeek-R1 model is provided below. We apply the same structure to other open-source thinking models, with slight adjustments for model-specific input and output formats.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt example for DeepSeek-R1:</span></p><span id="A5.p2.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A5.p2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_align_left ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;|begin_of_sentence|&gt;Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{}.
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_align_left ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;|User|&gt;[Question]&lt;|Assistant|&gt;&lt;think&gt;
</span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Example of a incorrect First Step</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A6.F1" title="Figure F.1 ‣ Appendix F Example of a incorrect First Step ‣ Lost at the Beginning of Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.1</span></a> illustrates a case where the initial reasoning step is incorrect.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.F1" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A6.F1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="756.69" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 756.69" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,756.69) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 750.79 C 0 754.05 2.64 756.69 5.91 756.69 L 544.09 756.69 C 547.36 756.69 550 754.05 550 750.79 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 732.58 L 548.03 732.58 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 741.18)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A6.F1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A6.F1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Example of incorrect first step</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 13.78)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:51.09em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="707" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 707)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A6.F1.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question:<span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Four unit squares form a <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times 2</annotation></semantics></math> grid. Each of the 12 unit line segments forming the sides of the squares is colored either red or blue in such a way that each unit square has 2 red sides and 2 blue sides. One example is shown below (red is solid, blue is dashed). Find the number of such colorings.</span></span></span>
<span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">[asy]
size(4cm);
defaultpen(linewidth(1.2));
draw((0, 0) – (2, 0) – (2, 1));
draw((0, 1) – (1, 1) – (1, 2) – (2,2));
draw((0, 0) – (0, 1), dotted);
draw((1, 0) – (1, 1) – (2, 1) – (2, 2), dotted);
draw((0, 1) – (0, 2) – (1, 2), dotted);
[/asy]</span></span>
<span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">First reason:<span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Alright, so I have this problem about coloring the sides of a 2x2 grid of squares. Each square has four sides, and each of these sides is colored either red or blue. The condition is that each individual square must have exactly two red sides and two blue sides. The question is asking for the number of such colorings.</span></span></span>
<span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">First, let me visualize the grid. It’s a 2x2 grid, so there are four squares arranged in a larger square. Each square has four sides, and <span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFCCCC;">each side is shared with another square except for the outermost sides</span>. But in the problem, it says there are 12 unit line segments forming the sides of the squares. Wait, let me check that: a 2x2 grid has 3 horizontal lines and 3 vertical lines, each of length 2 units. So, each horizontal line is divided into two segments, right? So, the total number of horizontal segments is 3 rows times 2 segments per row, which is 6, and similarly, the vertical segments are also 3 columns times 2 segments per column, which is another 6. So, 6 + 6 = 12 segments in total. Okay, that makes sense.</span></span>
<span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Each of these 12 segments can be colored either red or blue. However, the constraint is that each of the four squares must have exactly two red sides and two blue sides. So, even though each segment can be colored independently, we have these local constraints for each square.</span></span>
<span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">I think a good way to approach this problem is by considering each square and the possible colorings for its sides, then seeing how they can fit together without violating the constraints. However, since the coloring of one square’s side affects the adjacent squares, this could get complicated.</span></span>
<span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#CCFFCC;">Maybe I can model this as a graph</span></span>
<span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where each segment is a node, and the squares impose constraints on the nodes (i.e., exactly two red and two blue edges around each square). But I’m not too familiar with graph theory, so maybe that’s not the best approach.</span></span>
<span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Mistakes in first reasoning step:<span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.9.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFCCCC;">Mistake 1</span> incorrectly assumes that in a <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times 2</annotation></semantics></math> grid, each corner square has two shared and two unshared sides, without properly accounting for edge distribution. <span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.9.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#CCFFCC;">Mistake 2</span> introduces unnecessary abstraction by treating segments as “nodes,” which obscures the natural structure: the segments themselves are the edges whose colours we choose, and each square simply places a rule on its four incident edges. Working directly with those four constraints is far cleaner than introducing an extra level of abstraction.</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure F.1: </span>Example of incorrect first step.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Examples for Minor Perturbation</h2>

<figure id="A7.F1" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A7.F1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel" height="262.02" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 262.02" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,262.02) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 256.12 C 0 259.38 2.64 262.02 5.91 262.02 L 544.09 262.02 C 547.36 262.02 550 259.38 550 256.12 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#E8EEF7;" fill="#E8EEF7" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 237.91 L 548.03 237.91 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 246.51)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A7.F1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A7.F1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.F1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Original final conclusion</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 33.84)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:13.89em;--ltx-fo-depth:1.45em;font-size:10pt;" height="212.32" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 192.26)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A7.F1.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A7.F1.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.F1.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To solve the problem, we are given triangle <math id="A7.F1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ABC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ABC</annotation></semantics></math> with side lengths <math id="A7.F1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB=5</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A7.F1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BC=9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BC=9</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A7.F1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AC=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AC=10</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A7.F1.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.F1.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">[…]</span></span>
<span id="A7.F1.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.F1.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Step 4: Compute <math id="A7.F1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AP</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A7.F1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> lies on line segment <math id="A7.F1.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AD</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A7.F1.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> lies outside the circle, the point <math id="A7.F1.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> lies between <math id="A7.F1.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.F1.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore:</span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AP=DA-DP=\frac{325}{22}-\frac{2025}{286}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">325</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">22</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2025</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">286</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AP=DA-DP=\frac{325}{22}-\frac{2025}{286}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.F1.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.F1.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Find a common denominator:</span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{325}{22}=\frac{4225}{286}\Rightarrow AP=\frac{4225-2025}{286}=\frac{2200}{286}=\frac{100}{13}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">325</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">22</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4225</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">286</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4225</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2025</mn></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">286</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2200</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">286</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">13</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{325}{22}=\frac{4225}{286}\Rightarrow AP=\frac{4225-2025}{286}=\frac{2200}{286}=\frac{100}{13}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.F1.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.F1.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Final Step: Compute <math id="A7.F1.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m+n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m+n</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">The reduced form of <math id="A7.F1.pic1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AP</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A7.F1.pic1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{100}{13}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">13</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{100}{13}</annotation></semantics></math>, so:</span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=100,\quad n=13\Rightarrow m+n={\color[rgb]{1,0.5,0}\text{{\textbackslash boxed\lx@text@lbrace 113\lx@text@rbrace}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">13</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#FF8000">\boxed{113}</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=100,\quad n=13\Rightarrow m+n={\color[rgb]{1,0.5,0}\text{{\textbackslash boxed\lx@text@lbrace 113\lx@text@rbrace}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.F1.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.F1.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;">Final Answer: <span id="A7.F1.pic1.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">\boxed{113}</span><span id="A7.F1.pic1.2.6.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A7.F1.pic2" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel" height="225.35" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 225.35" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,225.35) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 219.45 C 0 222.71 2.64 225.35 5.91 225.35 L 544.09 225.35 C 547.36 225.35 550 222.71 550 219.45 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#DDEAF6;" fill="#DDEAF6" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 203.93 L 548.03 203.93 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 209.84)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A7.F1.pic2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A7.F1.pic2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.F1.pic2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">New correct first reason</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 16.47)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:12.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="178.35" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 175.66)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A7.F1.pic2.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A7.F1.pic2.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.F1.pic2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To solve the problem, we are given triangle <math id="A7.F1.pic2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ABC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ABC</annotation></semantics></math> with side lengths <math id="A7.F1.pic2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB=5</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A7.F1.pic2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BC=9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BC=9</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A7.F1.pic2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AC=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AC=10</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A7.F1.pic2.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.F1.pic2.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">[…]</span></span>
<span id="A7.F1.pic2.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.F1.pic2.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Step 4: Compute <math id="A7.F1.pic2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AP</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A7.F1.pic2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> lies on line segment <math id="A7.F1.pic2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AD</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A7.F1.pic2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> lies outside the circle, the point <math id="A7.F1.pic2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> lies between <math id="A7.F1.pic2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.F1.pic2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore:</span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AP=DA-DP=\frac{325}{22}-\frac{2025}{286}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">325</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">22</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2025</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">286</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AP=DA-DP=\frac{325}{22}-\frac{2025}{286}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.F1.pic2.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.F1.pic2.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Find a common denominator:</span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{325}{22}=\frac{4225}{286}\Rightarrow AP=\frac{4225-2025}{286}=\frac{2200}{286}=\frac{100}{13}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">325</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">22</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4225</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">286</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4225</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2025</mn></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">286</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2200</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">286</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">13</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{325}{22}=\frac{4225}{286}\Rightarrow AP=\frac{4225-2025}{286}=\frac{2200}{286}=\frac{100}{13}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.F1.pic2.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.F1.pic2.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Final Step: Compute <math id="A7.F1.pic2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m+n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m+n</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">The reduced form of <math id="A7.F1.pic2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AP</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A7.F1.pic2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{100}{13}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">13</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{100}{13}</annotation></semantics></math>, so:</span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=100,\quad n=13\Rightarrow m+n={\color[rgb]{1,0.5,0}\text{{113}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">13</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#FF8000">113</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=100,\quad n=13\Rightarrow m+n={\color[rgb]{1,0.5,0}\text{{113}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A7.F1.pic3" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel" height="225.35" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 225.35" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,225.35) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 219.45 C 0 222.71 2.64 225.35 5.91 225.35 L 544.09 225.35 C 547.36 225.35 550 222.71 550 219.45 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FDF0E6;" fill="#FDF0E6" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 203.93 L 548.03 203.93 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 209.84)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A7.F1.pic3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A7.F1.pic3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.F1.pic3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">New incorrect first reason</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 16.47)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:12.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="178.35" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 175.66)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A7.F1.pic3.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A7.F1.pic3.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.F1.pic3.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To solve the problem, we are given triangle <math id="A7.F1.pic3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ABC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ABC</annotation></semantics></math> with side lengths <math id="A7.F1.pic3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB=5</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A7.F1.pic3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BC=9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BC=9</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A7.F1.pic3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AC=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AC=10</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A7.F1.pic3.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.F1.pic3.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">[…]</span></span>
<span id="A7.F1.pic3.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.F1.pic3.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Step 4: Compute <math id="A7.F1.pic3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AP</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A7.F1.pic3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> lies on line segment <math id="A7.F1.pic3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AD</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A7.F1.pic3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> lies outside the circle, the point <math id="A7.F1.pic3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> lies between <math id="A7.F1.pic3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.F1.pic3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore:</span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AP=DA-DP=\frac{325}{22}-\frac{2025}{286}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">325</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">22</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2025</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">286</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AP=DA-DP=\frac{325}{22}-\frac{2025}{286}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.F1.pic3.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.F1.pic3.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Find a common denominator:</span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{325}{22}=\frac{4225}{286}\Rightarrow AP=\frac{4225-2025}{286}=\frac{2200}{286}=\frac{100}{13}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">325</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">22</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4225</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">286</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4225</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2025</mn></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">286</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2200</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">286</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">13</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{325}{22}=\frac{4225}{286}\Rightarrow AP=\frac{4225-2025}{286}=\frac{2200}{286}=\frac{100}{13}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.F1.pic3.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.F1.pic3.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Final Step: Compute <math id="A7.F1.pic3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m+n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m+n</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">The reduced form of <math id="A7.F1.pic3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AP</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A7.F1.pic3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{100}{13}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">13</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{100}{13}</annotation></semantics></math>, so:</span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=100,\quad n=13\Rightarrow m+n={\color[rgb]{1,0.5,0}\text{{103}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">13</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#FF8000">103</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=100,\quad n=13\Rightarrow m+n={\color[rgb]{1,0.5,0}\text{{103}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure G.1: </span>Illustration of a targeted perturbation to create correct and incorrect first reasoning steps, as discussed in §<a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Minor perturbation to the correct first step leads to significant loss ‣ 3 Lost at the beginning of reasoning ‣ Lost at the Beginning of Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>. The modified context is highlighted in orange.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
